      "heading": "Same student. Same question. A different mark.",
      "backgroundColor": "#453516",
      "callsToAction": [
        "First attempt",
        "After SJ method"
      ],
      "text": "HOW WE TEACH Same student. Same question. A different mark. You learn the way Cambridge wants answers written, then practise it on past papers marked against the mark scheme. the mark scheme has opinions Learn what each mark is for Before you write a word, the teacher shows you what the mark scheme rewards for that type of question. Write it under time Past-paper questions, timed, the way you will sit them in the exam hall. Get it marked It comes back marked the way a Cambridge examiner marks it. Fix the gap You see where each mark was lost and how to get it back. First attempt After SJ method",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
